# Project Vision: Mira Thai Massage Website
# File: .cursorrules — place at project root
# Chapter99 Solutions | Sydney, Australia

## 1. Goal
Build a professional PWA website for Mira Thai Massage
in Altona VIC, Australia. Target audience: local Australian
customers searching for Thai massage, remedial massage,
and HICAPS health fund services.

Business details:
- Name: Mira Thai Massage (MIRA Massage)
- Address: Level 1/76 Pier St, Altona VIC 3018
- Booking system: Receptionerapp (mira.book.receptionerapp.com)
- Services: Remedial, Relaxation, Deep Tissue, Couple Massage
- Health Fund: HICAPS accepted
- Language: English primary, Thai secondary

## 2. Technical Stack
- Framework: React + TypeScript + Vite
- Hosting: Vercel (auto-deploy from GitHub)
- Repo: github.com/chapter99info-cell/mira-v4-final
- Domain: mirathaimassage.com.au
- Styling: Tailwind CSS (no custom CSS unless critical)
- Animation: Framer Motion — subtle scroll fade only
- Icons: Lucide React
- NO Firebase — removed completely
- NO Supabase — static site, no database needed

## 3. Design System
Brand colors (use ONLY these — no new colors):
- Primary green: #2D5016 (dark forest green)
- Secondary gold: #C8A84B (warm gold)
- Background: #FFFFFF (white) / #F8F5F0 (warm off-white)
- Text primary: #1A1A1A
- Text muted: #6B7280
- CTA button: #2D5016 background, white text

Typography:
- Headings: font-serif (Georgia or similar)
- Body: font-sans (Inter or system)
- Thai text: Noto Sans Thai

Spacing system: use Tailwind defaults only (p-4, gap-6, etc.)

## 4. SEO + AI Friendly Rules (MANDATORY)
Every page MUST include:
- <title> with location: "Mira Thai Massage Altona | HICAPS"
- <meta name="description"> under 160 characters
- LocalBusiness JSON-LD schema with:
  name, address, telephone, openingHours, priceRange,
  acceptsReservations, hasMap, url
- FAQ section with minimum 5 Q&A pairs
- NAP consistent: Name/Address/Phone same on every page
- og:title, og:description, og:image for social sharing
- sitemap.xml and robots.txt at root

AI-friendly content rules:
- Answer questions directly in plain language
- Include "Do you accept health fund?" → "Yes, HICAPS"
- Include service descriptions as complete sentences
- Use structured headings (h1 → h2 → h3 only)

## 5. Security Rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
- No API keys of any kind in source code
- No Firebase imports — project uses zero Firebase
- .env file must exist in .gitignore
- No sensitive business data in client-side code
- console.log allowed only in development mode

## 6. Component Rules
Booking buttons:
- Primary CTA: "BOOK NOW / จองคิว" → links to Receptionerapp
- Gift voucher: "BUY GIFT VOUCHER / บัตรของขวัญ" → Receptionerapp
- Never build custom booking — always use Receptionerapp link

Image rules:
- Format: WebP preferred, JPG fallback
- Always include alt text in English and Thai
- Lazy loading on all images below the fold
- Hero image must load in < 1 second

Animation rules:
- Scroll-triggered fade-in: opacity 0 → 1, translateY 20px → 0
- Stagger delay: 0.1s between items maximum
- Duration: 0.4s maximum
- NO bounce, NO spin, NO complex keyframes

## 7. Development Workflow
- Check tailwind.config.ts for existing tokens FIRST
- New components go in /src/components/[name]/index.tsx
- Each component is self-contained with its own types
- git commit message format: "feat: [description]"
- Use Sonnet model — NEVER Opus unless explicitly asked
- NEVER use Multitask mode
- After every new feature: git add . && git commit && git push

## 8. Current Task
[REPLACE THIS: Describe the specific feature to build]
Example: "Add FAQ section below services with HICAPS question"
Example: "Add Google Maps embed near contact section"
Example: "Add client hero WebP to public/images/hero.webp"

## 9. Constraints
- Headlines: 8 words maximum
- Subheadlines: one sentence, specific outcome
- No flashy animations — professional spa feeling
- Button text: action-oriented (Book Now / จองเลย)
- Page must load under 3 seconds on 4G mobile
- All text must be readable at 14px minimum
- Maintain bilingual consistency: if English added, add Thai too
